@meta
id: 02-08
title: Undoing the undo
chapter: 02
type: lesson
skills: redo, undo
par: 56
minutes: 4
vscode: Ctrl+Y or Ctrl+Shift+Z
open: on-call.md

@brief
`u` one keystroke too far is a normal thing to do. You hold it down, the
text flies past, and you overshoot. `Ctrl-R` walks forward again: redo,
the exact mirror of undo.

The on call rota is being patched during the week. In order:

  1. Append ` (until Wednesday)` to the Primary line.

  2. Append ` (swap with Jo?)` to the Secondary line.

  3. Panic. Press `u` twice, which takes both of them off.

  4. The Primary change was right all along. Bring it back — and only it.

Then save. Primary keeps its note, Secondary is back to `Secondary: Sam`.

You typed the Primary note once. Type it a second time and you have
missed the point of the lesson, though the file will still be correct.

@keys
| `Ctrl-R` | redo — undo one undo |
| `u` | undo |
| `:redo` | the spelled out form of `Ctrl-R` |

@hints
Undo and redo move along the same line of changes. Two `u` presses put
you two steps back; you want to come forward one.
--
`Ctrl-R` is the control key with `r`, pressed in normal mode. Not `:r`,
which is something else entirely.
--
The order matters. Redo replays the oldest of the two undone changes
first, which is the Primary line — exactly the one you want.

@solution
    jj $ a  (until Wednesday) <Esc>
    j $ a  (swap with Jo?) <Esc>
    u u
    <Ctrl-R>
    ZZ

Undo and redo are a cursor moving along a list of states. `u` steps
towards the past, `Ctrl-R` steps towards the present, and neither of them
destroys anything by itself.

One rule to internalise now, because it explains a surprise later: the
moment you make a *new* change after undoing, the states ahead of you
stop being reachable by `Ctrl-R`. In most editors they are gone for good
at that point. In vim they are not gone, only off the path — and the last
lesson of this chapter is how to walk back onto it.

@start on-call.md
# On call this week

Primary: Priya
Secondary: Sam
Escalation: platform lead

@expected on-call.md
# On call this week

Primary: Priya (until Wednesday)
Secondary: Sam
Escalation: platform lead
